    {
      "id": "sec-2",
      "title": "Cosmology and Particle Physics",
      "module": "m42686",
      "est_minutes": 12,
      "locator": "CNXML module m42686",
      "objectives": [
        "Discuss the expansion of the universe.",
        "Explain the Big Bang."
      ],
      "misconceptions": [
        {
          "claim": "String theory is a confirmed theory of everything.",
          "correction": "It is a promising idea that is still being tested, and it is not part of the standard model."
        }
      ],
      "summary": [
        "Cosmology is the study of the character and evolution of the universe.",
        "The two most important features of the universe are the cosmological red shifts of its galaxies being proportional to distance and its cosmic microwave background (CMBR). Both support the notion that there was a gigantic explosion, known as the Big Bang that created the universe.",
        "Galaxies farther away than our local group have, on an average, a recessional velocity given by v = H 0 d,where d is the distance to the galaxy and H0 is the Hubble constant, taken to have the average value H0=20 km/s⋅Mly."
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "facts_inherited": true,
      "exam_links": [
        {
          "exam": "JAMB",
