      "misconceptions": [],
      "summary": [
        "High-temperature superconductors are materials that become superconducting at temperatures well above a few kelvin.",
        "The critical temperature Tc is the temperature below which a material is superconducting.",
        "Some high-temperature superconductors have verified Tc s above 125 K, and there are reports of Tc s as high as 250 K."
      ],
